\ Deadline: the pictures of the upstairs hall and the Robners' rooms. The
\ hall is one long corridor running east and west, 2 metres wide: the End of
\ Hallway (x -12 to -9) with the library to its north and the window at its
\ west end, then the halls outside George's room, the linen closet and Ms.
\ Dunbar's and the Robners' rooms, and the Top of Stairs (x 0 to 2.4), where
\ short halls run north and south and the stairs go down to the east. Each
\ hall picture stands the camera at its own place in the one corridor.

\ === pieces shared by these rooms ===

\ a window's frame on any four-sided wall patch a b c d (bottom left, bottom right, top right, top left), with panes columns by rows
: pane-grid ( a b c d columns rows -- )
	| a b c d columns rows |
	[ a b c d ] outline
	1 columns 1 do k
		k columns / to along
		a b along between d c along between segment
	loop
	1 rows 1 do k
		k rows / to up
		a d up between b c up between segment
	loop ;

\ the room behind an open door in a wall facing north or south at wall-z, centred at a distance east, the room toward into (1 north, -1 south): its floor and the door leaf swung into it; drawn before the wall hides what it should
: hall-door-beyond ( centre wall-z into -- )
	| centre wall-z into |
	centre 0.45 - to west
	centre 0.45 + to east
	0.1 pen!
	west 0 wall-z west 0 wall-z into 2.5 * + edge
	east 0 wall-z east 0 wall-z into 2.5 * + edge
	west 0 wall-z into 2.5 * + east 0 wall-z into 2.5 * + edge
	0.45 pen!
	[ [ west 0 wall-z ] [ west 0.3 + 0 wall-z into 0.84 * + ]
	  [ west 0.3 + 2.06 wall-z into 0.84 * + ] [ west 2.06 wall-z ] ] outline ;

\ a door's frame in a wall facing north or south at wall-z, centred at a distance east; shut, the door itself with its panels and knob
: hall-door ( centre wall-z open -- )
	| centre wall-z open |
	centre 0.45 - to west
	centre 0.45 + to east
	[ [ west 0 wall-z ] [ east 0 wall-z ] [ east 2.1 wall-z ] [ west 2.1 wall-z ] ] to opening
	open not if
		opening 0 fill
		0.3 pen!
		0 2 1 do across
			0 2 1 do high
				across 0.36 * west 0.09 + + to panel-west
				high 0.95 * 0.12 + to panel-bottom
				[ [ panel-west panel-bottom wall-z ] [ panel-west 0.3 + panel-bottom wall-z ]
				  [ panel-west 0.3 + panel-bottom 0.8 + wall-z ] [ panel-west panel-bottom 0.8 + wall-z ] ] outline
			loop
		loop
		0.85 pen!
		[ east 0.12 - 1.0 wall-z ] [ 1 0 0 ] [ 0 1 0 ] 0.022 detail-scale * 8 circle-points outline
	then
	0.6 pen!
	[ [ west 0 wall-z ] [ west 2.1 wall-z ] [ east 2.1 wall-z ] [ east 0 wall-z ] ] path
	0.25 pen!
	[ [ west 0.07 - 0 wall-z ] [ west 0.07 - 2.17 wall-z ] [ east 0.07 + 2.17 wall-z ] [ east 0.07 + 0 wall-z ] ] path ;

\ fill a stretch of a hall side wall black between two heights, in half-metre strips so that the strips behind the camera are the only ones left unfilled
: hall-wall-strips ( west east bottom top z -- )
	| west east bottom top z |
	east west - 0.5 / round-up 1 max2 to n-strips
	east west - n-strips / to width
	0 n-strips 1 do k
		k width * west + to from
		from width + to onto
		[ [ from bottom z ] [ onto bottom z ] [ onto top z ] [ from top z ] ] 0 fill
	loop ;

\ fill one of the hall's side walls black from x -12 to 2.4, leaving the openings given as [ west east top ] open
: hall-wall-fill ( z openings -- )
	| z openings |
	-12 to from
	0 openings size 1 do k
		openings k @i spread to top to east to west
		from west 0 2.8 z hall-wall-strips
		west east top 2.8 z hall-wall-strips
		east to from
	loop
	from 2.4 0 2.8 z hall-wall-strips ;

\ a horizontal line along one of the hall's side walls from west to east, broken by the openings given as [ west east ] pairs
: hall-wall-run ( west east y z openings -- )
	| west east y z openings |
	west to from
	0 openings size 1 do k
		openings k @i to gap
		from y z gap first y z edge
		gap second to from
	loop
	from y z east y z edge ;

\ the long carpet runner down the middle of the hall, its border and its pattern
: hall-runner ( west east -- )
	| west east |
	0.14 pen!
	[ [ west 0 -0.45 ] [ east 0 -0.45 ] [ east 0 0.45 ] [ west 0 0.45 ] ] outline
	0.07 pen!
	[ [ west 0.06 + 0 -0.38 ] [ east 0.06 - 0 -0.38 ] [ east 0.06 - 0 0.38 ] [ west 0.06 + 0 0.38 ] ] outline
	west 0.6 + east 0.6 do x
		[ [ x 0 -0.25 ] [ x 0.25 + 0 0 ] [ x 0 0.25 ] [ x 0.25 - 0 0 ] ] outline
	loop ;

\ a light hanging from the hall ceiling
: hall-lamp ( x -- )
	| x |
	[ x 2.62 0 ] 0.7 0.18 glow
	0.5 pen!
	x 2.8 0 x 2.68 0 edge
	x 2.62 0 0.12 8 ring outline
	x 2.68 0 0.05 8 ring outline ;

\ the whole upstairs hall: floor, runner, walls, doors, the end window and the view through it, the halls off the Top of Stairs and the stairwell
: upstairs-hall ( -- )
	\ first what lies beyond the side walls, seen only through their openings
	[ -10.7 1.2 3.5 ] 1.8 0.14 glow
	0.08 pen!
	[ -12 0 1 ] [ -8.8 0 1 ] [ -8.8 0 5 ] [ -12 0 5 ] 7 8 grid
	0.65 pen!
	-11.3 0 1.15 -9.95 0.08 2.2 solid-box
	0.25 pen!
	[ [ -11.2 0.08 1.3 ] [ -10.66 0.08 1.3 ] [ -10.66 0.08 2.05 ] [ -11.2 0.08 2.05 ] ] outline
	[ [ -10.56 0.08 1.3 ] [ -10.05 0.08 1.3 ] [ -10.05 0.08 2.05 ] [ -10.56 0.08 2.05 ] ] outline
	0.2 pen!
	-5.2 0 1.6 -3.8 0 1.6 edge
	-5.2 0 1 -5.2 0 1.6 edge
	-3.8 0 1 -3.8 0 1.6 edge
	0 5 1 do shelf
		shelf 0.42 * 0.2 + to board
		0.35 pen!
		-5.2 board 1.25 -3.8 board 1.25 edge
		-5.2 board 1.6 -3.8 board 1.6 edge
		0.25 pen!
		0 4 1 do pile
			pile 0.34 * -5.1 + to pile-west
			shelf 7 * pile + hash-fraction to chance
			chance 0.1 * 0.14 + to pile-height
			chance 0.06 * to pile-shift
			[ [ pile-west pile-shift + board 1.26 ] [ pile-west 0.26 + pile-shift + board 1.26 ]
			  [ pile-west 0.26 + pile-shift + board pile-height + 1.26 ] [ pile-west pile-shift + board pile-height + 1.26 ] ] outline
			0.12 pen!
			pile-west pile-shift + board pile-height 0.5 * + 1.26 pile-west 0.26 + pile-shift + board pile-height 0.5 * + 1.26 edge
			0.25 pen!
		loop
	loop
	:george-door :open flag? if -7.5 -1 -1 hall-door-beyond then
	:dunbar-door :open flag? if -1.5 -1 -1 hall-door-beyond then
	:master-bedroom-door :open flag? if -1.5 1 1 hall-door-beyond then
	[ 1 -1 ] ( side |
		0.2 pen!
		0.3 0 side 0.3 0 side 4 * edge
		1.8 0 side 1.8 0 side 4 * edge
		0.3 2.8 side 0.3 2.8 side 4 * edge
		1.8 2.8 side 1.8 2.8 side 4 * edge
		0.12 pen!
		0.3 0.9 side 0.3 0.9 side 4 * edge
		1.8 0.9 side 1.8 0.9 side 4 * edge
		0.15 pen!
		[ [ 0.3 0 side 4 * ] [ 1.8 0 side 4 * ] [ 1.8 2.8 side 4 * ] [ 0.3 2.8 side 4 * ] ] outline
		0.3 pen!
		[ [ 0.65 0 side 4 * ] [ 0.65 2.05 side 4 * ] [ 1.45 2.05 side 4 * ] [ 1.45 0 side 4 * ] ] path
		[ 1.05 2.6 side 2.5 * ] 0.6 0.1 glow
		0.06 pen!
		0.45 1.8 0.15 do x x 0 side x 0 side 4 * edge loop
		0.14 pen!
		[ [ 0.6 0 side ] [ 1.5 0 side ] [ 1.5 0 side 3.9 * ] [ 0.6 0 side 3.9 * ] ] outline
	) each
	\ then the side walls, solid, and the hall in front of them
	[ [ -11.2 -10.2 2.2 ] [ -5.2 -3.8 2.2 ] [ -1.95 -1.05 2.1 ] [ 0.3 1.8 2.8 ] ] to north-gaps
	[ [ -7.95 -7.05 2.1 ] [ -1.95 -1.05 2.1 ] [ 0.3 1.8 2.8 ] ] to south-gaps
	1 north-gaps hall-wall-fill
	-1 south-gaps hall-wall-fill
	0.05 pen!
	-0.9 0.95 0.15 do z -12 0 z 2.4 0 z edge loop
	-11.7 2.3 hall-runner
	[ [ -11.2 -10.2 ] [ -5.2 -3.8 ] [ -1.95 -1.05 ] [ 0.3 1.8 ] ] to north-openings
	[ [ -7.95 -7.05 ] [ -1.95 -1.05 ] [ 0.3 1.8 ] ] to south-openings
	0.42 pen!
	-12 2.4 0 1 north-openings hall-wall-run
	-12 2.4 0 -1 south-openings hall-wall-run
	-12 2.4 2.8 1 [ [ 0.3 1.8 ] ] hall-wall-run
	-12 2.4 2.8 -1 [ [ 0.3 1.8 ] ] hall-wall-run
	0.14 pen!
	-12 2.4 0.9 1 north-openings hall-wall-run
	-12 2.4 0.9 -1 south-openings hall-wall-run
	0.1 pen!
	-12 2.4 2.5 1 [ [ 0.3 1.8 ] ] hall-wall-run
	-12 2.4 2.5 -1 [ [ 0.3 1.8 ] ] hall-wall-run
	\ the west end wall and its window, trees and the lake beyond
	[ [ -12 0 -1 ] [ -12 0 1 ] [ -12 2.8 1 ] [ -12 2.8 -1 ] ] 0 fill
	0.42 pen!
	[ [ -12 0 -1 ] [ -12 0 1 ] [ -12 2.8 1 ] [ -12 2.8 -1 ] ] outline
	[ [ -12 0.8 -0.6 ] [ -12 0.8 0.6 ] [ -12 2.3 0.6 ] [ -12 2.3 -0.6 ] ] 0.04 fill
	0.1 pen!
	-12.01 1.35 -0.6 -12.01 1.35 0.6 edge
	-12.01 1.28 -0.6 -12.01 1.28 0.6 edge
	0.16 pen!
	[ [ -0.45 1.7 0.13 ] [ -0.1 1.95 0.15 ] [ 0.3 1.62 0.12 ] ] ( tree |
		tree spread to radius to height to across
		[ 0 14 1 do k
			k 14 / TAU * to angle
			across 17 * k + hash-fraction 0.35 * 0.8 + radius * to reach
			[ -12.02 height angle sin reach * + across angle cos reach * + ]
		loop ] outline
		-12.02 1.35 across -12.02 height radius 0.8 * - across edge
	) each
	[ -12 1.55 0 ] 1.3 0.3 glow
	0.8 pen!
	[ -12 0.8 -0.6 ] [ -12 0.8 0.6 ] [ -12 2.3 0.6 ] [ -12 2.3 -0.6 ] 2 3 pane-grid
	0.1 pen!
	[ [ -12 0 -0.55 ] [ -12 0 0.55 ] [ -10.6 0 0.8 ] [ -10.6 0 -0.8 ] ] 0.05 fill
	[ -12 0 -0.55 ] [ -12 0 0.55 ] [ -10.6 0 0.8 ] [ -10.6 0 -0.8 ] 6 hatch
	\ the frames of the library doorway, its door knocked down, and of the linen closet; the doors of George's, Ms. Dunbar's and the Robners' rooms
	0.6 pen!
	[ [ -11.2 0 1 ] [ -11.2 2.2 1 ] [ -10.2 2.2 1 ] [ -10.2 0 1 ] ] path
	0.35 pen!
	-10.3 1.0 1 -10.3 1.25 1 edge
	0.6 pen!
	[ [ -5.2 0 1 ] [ -5.2 2.2 1 ] [ -3.8 2.2 1 ] [ -3.8 0 1 ] ] path
	-7.5 -1 :george-door :open flag? hall-door
	-1.5 -1 :dunbar-door :open flag? hall-door
	-1.5 1 :master-bedroom-door :open flag? hall-door
	\ the corners where the short halls leave the Top of Stairs
	0.45 pen!
	[ 1 -1 ] ( side |
		0.3 0 side 0.3 2.8 side edge
		1.8 0 side 1.8 2.8 side edge
	) each
	\ the stairwell going down to the east, its banisters and newel posts
	0.3 pen!
	0 12 1 do step
		step 0.28 * 2.4 + to tread
		step 0.18 * negate to height
		tread height -0.85 tread height 0.85 edge
	loop
	[ 1 -1 ] ( side |
		0.55 pen!
		2.4 0.95 side 0.9 * 5.76 -1.21 side 0.9 * edge
		2.35 0 side 0.9 * 0.06 - 2.47 1.05 side 0.9 * 0.06 + solid-box
	) each
	0.42 pen!
	2.4 2.8 1 6.2 2.8 1 edge
	2.4 2.8 -1 6.2 2.8 -1 edge
	-9.2 hall-lamp
	-4.5 hall-lamp
	1.05 hall-lamp ;

\ === the hall ===

\ looking west from the head of the stairs down the whole length of the hall
: stair-top-picture ( -- )
	3.1 1.7 -0.65 -0.95 -0.07 230 new-picture
	level-camera!
	[ 1.05 2.6 0 ] lamp!
	[ [ [ 1.0 0 0.2 ] 2.6 ] [ [ -0.6 0 -0.2 ] 1.9 ] [ [ 1.1 0 2.4 ] 2.8 ] ] spots!
	upstairs-hall ;

\ just west of the stairs, between Ms. Dunbar's door and the master bedroom door
: corridor-1-picture ( -- )
	0.6 1.65 0.1 -1.62 -0.05 270 new-picture
	[ -1.5 2.6 0 ] lamp!
	[ [ [ -2.8 0 0.25 ] 1.8 ] [ [ -4.4 0 -0.3 ] 1.4 ] [ [ -6.2 0 0.2 ] 1.6 ] ] spots!
	upstairs-hall ;

\ the middle of the hall by the linen closet, looking toward the window
: corridor-2-picture ( -- )
	-2.4 1.65 -0.25 -1.46 -0.05 270 new-picture
	[ -4.5 2.6 0 ] lamp!
	[ [ [ -5.4 0 -0.2 ] 1.4 ] [ [ -6.8 0 0.3 ] 1.8 ] [ [ -3.9 0 0.35 ] 1.9 ] ] spots!
	upstairs-hall ;

\ outside George's room, the window at the end of the hall ahead
: corridor-3-picture ( -- )
	-5.6 1.65 0.2 -1.66 -0.05 270 new-picture
	[ -12 1.6 0 ] lamp!
	[ [ [ -8.3 0 0.3 ] 1.8 ] [ [ -9.6 0 -0.3 ] 1.4 ] [ [ -7.0 0 0.45 ] 2.0 ] ] spots!
	upstairs-hall ;

\ the west end of the hall: the window ahead, the library doorway to the right
: corridor-4-picture ( -- )
	-8.6 1.65 -0.7 -1.08 -0.06 260 new-picture
	[ -12 1.6 0 ] lamp!
	[ [ [ -11.3 0 -0.3 ] 1.2 ] [ [ -9.9 0 0.1 ] 2.2 ] [ [ -11.0 0 0.45 ] 1.8 ] ] spots!
	upstairs-hall ;

\ === pieces for the rooms off the hall ===

\ a standing spot and the heading that faces a point x z on the floor, as spots! takes them
: upper-heading ( spot x z -- pair )
	| spot x z |
	[ spot x spot first - z spot 2 @i - atan2 ] ;

\ a metal balcony railing from one point to another at floor height: top and bottom rails and the balusters between
: upper-railing ( a b count -- )
	| a b count |
	a spread to az to ay to ax
	b spread to bz to by to bx
	0.75 pen!
	ax ay 1.02 + az bx by 1.02 + bz edge
	0.4 pen!
	ax ay 0.08 + az bx by 0.08 + bz edge
	0.32 pen!
	0 count 1 + 1 do k
		k count / to along
		ax bx ax - along * + to x
		az bz az - along * + to z
		x ay 0.08 + z x ay 1.02 + z edge
	loop ;

\ a fruit tree's crown facing the camera: a ragged mass of foliage hiding what is behind it, clumps of leaves and a few fruit inside it, and the trunk forking up from the ground into it
: upper-tree-crown ( x y z radius ground seed -- )
	| x y z radius ground seed |
	z view@z - to toward-z
	view@x x - to toward-x
	toward-x sq toward-z sq + sqrt to distance
	[ toward-z distance / 0 toward-x distance / ] to across
	0.12 pen!
	[ -1 1 ] ( side | x side 0.1 * across first * + ground z side 0.1 * across 2 @i * + x side 0.06 * across first * + y radius 0.4 * - z side 0.06 * across 2 @i * + edge ) each
	[ -1 1 ] ( side | x y radius 0.4 * - z x side radius 0.45 * * across first * + y radius 0.1 * - z side radius 0.45 * * across 2 @i * + edge ) each
	[ 0 24 1 do k
		k 24 / TAU * to angle
		seed 31 * k + hash-fraction 0.3 * 0.78 + radius * to reach
		[ x angle cos reach * across first * + y angle sin reach * 0.75 * + z angle cos reach * across 2 @i * + ]
	loop ] to crown
	crown 0 fill
	0.45 pen!
	crown outline
	0.2 pen!
	0 4 1 do k
		seed 7 * k + hash-fraction 1.2 * radius * 0.6 radius * - to offset-across
		seed 5 * k + 3 + hash-fraction 0.8 * radius * 0.4 radius * - to offset-up
		[ x offset-across across first * + y offset-up + z offset-across across 2 @i * + ] to clump
		[ 0 6 1 do step
			step 5 / 3.1416 * to angle
			[ clump first angle cos radius 0.22 * * across first * + clump 1 @i angle sin radius 0.18 * * + clump 2 @i angle cos radius 0.22 * * across 2 @i * + ]
		loop ] path
	loop
	0.55 pen!
	0 5 1 do k
		seed 13 * k + hash-fraction 1.3 * radius * 0.65 radius * - to offset-across
		seed 17 * k + hash-fraction 1.0 * radius * 0.5 radius * - to offset-up
		[ x offset-across across first * + y offset-up + z offset-across across 2 @i * + ] across [ 0 1 0 ] 0.05 6 circle-points outline
	loop ;

\ the top of the wooden ladder leaning on a railing: its rails rising from the ground below to just above the rail, and the rungs between
: upper-ladder-top ( x rail-z ground foot-z -- )
	| x rail-z ground foot-z |
	0.75 pen!
	[ -0.22 0.22 ] ( side | x side + ground foot-z x side + 1.35 rail-z 0.05 + edge ) each
	0.6 pen!
	0 12 1 do k
		k 11 / to along
		ground 1.35 ground - along * + to height
		foot-z rail-z 0.05 + foot-z - along * + to z
		x 0.22 - height z x 0.22 + height z edge
	loop ;

\ rows of rose bushes on the ground far below, seen from above: dark mounds with a lit rim and a few blooms, in rows running east and west
: upper-rose-rows ( west east south north ground -- )
	| west east south north ground |
	south north 1.1 do z
		west east 0.9 do x
			x 13 * z 7 * + hash-fraction to chance
			x 0.9 / round z 1.1 / round + 2 mod 0.45 * to stagger
			[ x chance 0.2 * + stagger + ground 0.3 + z chance 0.3 * + ] to centre
			[ 0 11 1 do k
				k 11 / TAU * to angle
				chance 29 * k + hash-fraction 0.35 * 0.8 + 0.34 * to reach
				[ centre first angle cos reach * + centre 1 @i centre 2 @i angle sin reach * + ]
			loop ] to mound
			mound 0 fill
			0.24 pen!
			mound outline
			0.65 pen!
			0 2 1 do k
				chance 17 * k + hash-fraction TAU * to angle
				chance 23 * k + hash-fraction 0.18 * to spread-out
				[ centre first angle cos spread-out * + centre 1 @i 0.02 + centre 2 @i angle sin spread-out * + ] [ 1 0 0 ] [ 0 0 1 ] 0.045 5 circle-points outline
			loop
		loop
	loop ;

\ a cobweb in a corner: threads fanning from the corner and rings across them
: upper-cobweb ( corner across down -- )
	| corner across down |
	0.18 pen!
	[ 0 0.35 0.7 1 ] ( t | corner corner across down t between ' + 2 nmap segment ) each
	[ 0.3 0.6 ] ( ring | [ 0 0.35 0.7 1 ] ( t | corner across down t between ( ring * ) map ' + 2 nmap ) map path ) each ;

\ === the Library Balcony ===

\ the bare balcony over the rose garden: the railing, the view of the roses, the north lawn and the lake, the window back into the library, the ladder's top when it leans here, and McNabb below
: library-balcony-picture ( -- )
	1.6 1.7 0.35 -1.0 -0.2 230 new-picture
	[ -8 9 40 ] lamp!
	[ [ -0.6 0 1.0 ] 1.6 0.35 upper-heading [ -1.8 0 0.7 ] 1.6 0.35 upper-heading ] spots!
	\ the lake and its shore far off, the north lawn, the roses directly below
	1.6 pen!
	-45 -3.5 45 12 -3.5 45 edge
	0.7 pen!
	0 9 1 do k k 1.3 * 47 + to z -45 -3.5 z 12 -3.5 z edge loop
	[ -16 3 60 ] 7 0.2 glow
	0.06 pen!
	[ -24 -3.5 12 ] [ 8 -3.5 12 ] [ 8 -3.5 44 ] [ -24 -3.5 44 ] 4 10 grid
	0.13 pen!
	-7 4 4.6 12 -3.5 upper-rose-rows
	0.12 pen!
	-7 -3.5 2.4 7 -3.5 2.4 edge
	-7 -3.5 11.5 7 -3.5 11.5 edge
	:gardener :rose-garden inside? if [ 3.2 -3.5 8.5 ] 2.9 gardener-figure then
	:gardener :north-lawn inside? if [ -4 -3.5 26 ] 3.3 gardener-figure then
	\ the balcony: its floor hiding the garden beneath it, the house wall and the window to the library, the railing
	:ladder-flag state if -0.2 1.8 -3.5 2.9 upper-ladder-top then
	:ladder-flag state if [ [ -1.2 0 0.9 ] [ 0.8 0 0.9 ] [ 0.8 0 1.8 ] [ -1.2 0 1.8 ] ] 0 fill then
	0.1 pen!
	[ -3 0 0.3 ] [ 2 0 0.3 ] [ 2 0 1.8 ] [ -3 0 1.8 ] 1 11 grid
	0.5 pen!
	[ [ -3 0 0 ] [ -3 0 1.8 ] [ 2 0 1.8 ] ] path
	-3 0 0 2 0 0 edge
	-3 0 0 -3 3.2 0 edge
	0.25 pen!
	-3 3.2 0 1.2 3.2 0 edge
	0.45 pen!
	[ [ -0.4 0.003 1.45 ] [ 1 0 0 ] [ 0 0 1 ] 0.05 detail-scale * 6 circle-points
	  [ 0.2 0.003 1.1 ] [ 1 0 0 ] [ 0 0 1 ] 0.04 detail-scale * 6 circle-points ] ( spot | spot 0.12 fill ) each
	0.7 pen!
	[ -2.6 0 0 ] [ -1.2 0 0 ] [ -1.2 2.4 0 ] [ -2.6 2.4 0 ] 2 4 pane-grid
	:library-balcony-door :open flag? if
		[ [ -2.6 0 0 ] [ -1.9 0 0 ] [ -1.9 2.4 0 ] [ -2.6 2.4 0 ] ] 0 fill
		[ -2.25 1.2 -1.5 ] 1.2 0.12 glow
	then
	[ -3 0 1.8 ] [ 2 0 1.8 ] 40 upper-railing
	[ -3 0 0 ] [ -3 0 1.8 ] 16 upper-railing
	0.9 pen!
	-0.35 1.02 1.8 -0.1 1.02 1.8 edge
	:library-balcony-door :open flag? if
		[ [ -2.6 0 0 ] [ -2.2 0 0.6 ] [ -2.2 2.4 0.6 ] [ -2.6 2.4 0 ] ] 0.03 fill
		0.6 pen!
		[ -2.6 0 0 ] [ -2.2 0 0.6 ] [ -2.2 2.4 0.6 ] [ -2.6 2.4 0 ] 1 4 pane-grid
	then ;

\ === the Upstairs Closet ===

\ a small bottle standing on a surface at height y: a solid body outlined along its silhouette, a lit label, its neck and cap brighter
: upper-bottle ( x y z radius height -- )
	| x y z radius height |
	y height + to shoulder
	radius 0.45 * to neck
	z view@z - to toward-z
	view@x x - to toward-x
	toward-x sq toward-z sq + sqrt to distance
	toward-z distance / to across-x
	toward-x distance / to across-z
	[ x across-x radius * - y z across-z radius * - ] to left-foot
	[ x across-x radius * + y z across-z radius * + ] to right-foot
	[ x across-x radius * + shoulder z across-z radius * + ] to right-top
	[ x across-x radius * - shoulder z across-z radius * - ] to left-top
	x shoulder z radius 10 ring to rim
	[ left-foot right-foot right-top left-top ] 0 fill
	rim 0 fill
	[ left-foot left-top 0.3 between right-foot right-top 0.3 between right-foot right-top 0.72 between left-foot left-top 0.72 between ] 0.22 fill
	0.75 pen!
	x y z radius 10 ring outline
	rim outline
	left-foot left-top segment
	right-foot right-top segment
	0.9 pen!
	x shoulder z neck 8 ring outline
	x shoulder 0.035 + z neck 8 ring outline
	[ -1 1 ] ( side | x side neck * across-x * + shoulder z side neck * across-z * + x side neck * across-x * + shoulder 0.035 + z side neck * across-z * + edge ) each ;

\ the shallow linen closet off the hall: its shelves of folded linens, rolled towels and toilet articles, seen close from its opening
: upstairs-closet-picture ( -- )
	0 1.6 -1.7 0 -0.2 260 new-picture
	[ 0 2.6 -1.6 ] lamp!
	[ ] spots!
	0.12 pen!
	[ [ -0.7 0 0.6 ] [ 0.7 0 0.6 ] [ 0.7 2.2 0.6 ] [ -0.7 2.2 0.6 ] ] outline
	-0.7 0 0 -0.7 0 0.6 edge
	0.7 0 0 0.7 0 0.6 edge
	-0.7 2.2 0 -0.7 2.2 0.6 edge
	0.7 2.2 0 0.7 2.2 0.6 edge
	0 5 1 do shelf
		shelf 0.42 * 0.12 + to board
		0.45 pen!
		-0.7 board 0 0.7 board 0.6 solid-box
		board 0.03 + to top
		shelf 2 = if
			0 5 1 do k
				k 0.26 * -0.55 + to x
				shelf 11 * k + hash-fraction to chance
				0.035 detail-scale * to radius
				chance 0.08 * 0.1 + detail-scale * to height
				x top 0.3 radius height upper-bottle
			loop
		else shelf 3 = if
			0 4 1 do k
				k 0.34 * -0.52 + to x
				0.07 detail-scale * to radius
				0.55 pen!
				[ x top radius + 0.12 ] [ 1 0 0 ] [ 0 1 0 ] radius 12 circle-points to roll
				roll 0.05 fill
				roll outline
				[ x top radius + 0.12 ] [ 1 0 0 ] [ 0 1 0 ] radius 0.45 * 10 circle-points outline
			loop
		else
			0 3 1 do k
				k 0.44 * -0.64 + to x
				shelf 5 * k + hash-fraction to chance
				chance 0.14 * 0.14 + to height
				0.5 pen!
				x top 0.08 x 0.4 + top height + 0.5 solid-box
				0.25 pen!
				0 4 1 do fold
					fold 1 + height * 5 / top + to crease
					x crease 0.08 x 0.4 + crease 0.08 edge
				loop
			loop
		then then
	loop
	0.65 pen!
	[ [ -0.7 0 0 ] [ -0.7 2.2 0 ] [ 0.7 2.2 0 ] [ 0.7 0 0 ] ] path
	0.3 pen!
	[ [ -0.78 0 0 ] [ -0.78 2.28 0 ] [ 0.78 2.28 0 ] [ 0.78 0 0 ] ] path ;

